{"id": "idaho-1", "headline": "Idaho lawmakers plan bill to classify e-motos as motorcycles", "source": "Idaho Capital Sun", "url": "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/11/20/idaho-legislature-may-clamp-down-on-high-powered-e-motorbikes-amid-injuries/", "published": "2026-11-20", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Rep. Brooke Green, a Boise Democrat, and Sen. Treg Bernt, a Meridian Republican, said Thursday they will introduce a bill next session to classify high-powered e-motos as motorcycles, the Idaho Capital Sun reports. The vehicles can exceed 30 mph but are often sold as e-bikes. Riders would need a driver's license with a motorcycle endorsement, and the vehicles would have to meet street-legal requirements. Idaho emergency rooms have had nearly 1,900 visits this year tied to electric mobility devices such as e-bikes and e-scooters, including 306 boys aged 11 to 15. Boise acted earlier this year, and Nampa passed rules in September barring faster e-motos from sidewalks and greenbelts.", "Source: Idaho Capital Sun"], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110000010110011011110011011001111111", "10000010100100010100110101010110001000001", "10111010100100100111100110010100101011101", "10111010000111000101001100100011001011101", "10111010101111001111110111111010001011101", "10000010101001100001001000110001101000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000100000100111110110001111000000000", "11010011000101111001010101001000101110110", "00110100010110101010100000100100111000011", "11010110101000001101000011101001010011110", "00100000100110111101011101011001101100101", "01000111010000010000110011010111011001011", "11100101101101011101001010000001110001100", "10101111110100000010101100000100101010111", "11110001101101110110011101001101100111010", "01001110110010100101111100110101110001010", "01000001100101100000000100001110011101101", "10000111000010100010110001100000100110111", "10100101001100110110111010100110011111000", "10111010101110001111110011111000001101110